                <pb facs="0136" n="124" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg124"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/37<hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >3/17</hi>a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Haiti</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Mayer</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-01T13:00:00-04:00">June 1, 1940—1 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>78. From the Under Secretary. Department’s No. 77, May 29, 3 p.m. Lt. Col. N.
                    Randolph, U. S. Army, and Colonel P. A. del Valle, U.S.M.C., have been
                    designated respectively by the War and Navy Departments to undertake the
                    proposed conversations in Port-au-Prince with the Haitian authorities. The date
                    of their arrival in Port-au-Prince is not yet fixed, as they will go first to
                    Habana, arriving June 7, there to undertake similar conversations with the
                    appropriate Cuban authorities. They will advise you through the Embassy in
                    Habana of the date and hour of their arrival in Port-au-Prince. Following the
                    termination of their conversations in Port-au-Prince they will proceed to Ciudad
                    Trujillo. [Welles.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
